{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unpaid-sanctified-aardvark","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\n\n`rebar link <source> <target> supersedes` refuses when `<source>` is closed, but the\ndisposition-close gate that CONSUMES `supersedes` links accepts a closed source. A story\ndecomposed into slices can therefore never close with `--class superseded` without an\noperator force, because the slices that replaced it close before it does.\n\n## Evidence (measured on origin/main 38f8587f65d)\n\n- `src/rebar/graph/_links.py:260-264` refuses any link whose source ticket is `closed`. The\n  guard is unconditional across all 7 relations in `CANONICAL_RELATIONS` (`_links.py:21-35`).\n  The very next guard (`:266-271`) narrows to `depends_on` for its target check, so the module\n  narrows by relation where narrowing is intended — this one does not.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:33-50` `_is_live_ticket` counts a ticket as a usable\n  replacement unless it is archived or deleted. A `closed` ticket PASSES.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py:29-76` `replacement_of` reads the subject's\n  outbound `duplicates` link or an inbound `supersedes` link, filtering both through\n  `_is_live_ticket`. So the reader expects closed sources the writer forbids.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py:21` `REASON_REQUIRED_CLASSES` excludes\n  `superseded`, so `--reason` cannot substitute. A replacement link is the ONLY evidence that\n  satisfies `superseded`.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:112-145` and `:184-198` — the gate's disposition exemption\n  calls `close_disposition.verdict` and returns `ok: True` with verdict `disposition`.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nObserved closing story `a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711`, whose scope was absorbed by three now-closed\nsibling slices (`43bd-2668-aa3e-4950`, `f7bd-e80c-...`, `742d-3980-...`):\n\n1. `rebar link 43bd-2668-aa3e-4950 a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711 supersedes`\n   -> `cannot create supersedes link - source ticket is closed`.\n2. Naming the parent epic instead -> rejected as `redundant link (ancestor-descendant)`.\n3. `rebar transition a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711 open closed --class superseded`\n   -> `plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`.\n\nThere is no reciprocal `superseded_by` relation, and only `relates_to` writes a reciprocal, so\nthe subject cannot record the relationship from its own side either. The one writable shape,\n`a256 -duplicates-> 43bd`, misstates a three-way decomposition as a duplicate.\n\n`a256` was closed with an operator force on 2026-10-30 to unblock its epic; that force is the\ndurable audit signal that this gate path was unreachable.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `rebar link <closed-source> <live-target> supersedes` succeeds, and the link\n      reduces to a `supersedes` entry on the closed source's `deps`.\n- [ ] AC2: The closed-source guard is NARROWED, not removed: `blocks` and `depends_on` still\n      refuse a closed source, each with a test.\n- [ ] AC3: With that link present, `transition <target> open closed --class superseded` passes\n      the plan-review close gate with verdict `disposition`, WITHOUT `--force`, and signs a\n      `completion-verifier: DISPOSITION superseded` manifest naming the replacement.\n- [ ] AC4: The writer's accepted-source rule and the reader's `_is_live_ticket` rule agree;\n      a test asserts a source the reader would accept is one the writer will create.\n- [ ] AC5: `make verify` passes.\n","id":"868c-dd56-d464-44bf","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["gate","disposition"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"supersedes refuses a closed source, stranding superseded closes"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793393236708319072,"uuid":"4c0954a2-29df-4b7f-a670-e12ab2c9a585"}